{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>And he gave him Rachel.</b> And if you ask: how did Jacob our father marry two sisters during their lifetimes — did he not keep the entire Torah? One may answer: our Rabbis said that a convert who converts is like a newborn child. And another interpretation: Leah and Rachel were from two wives, and the children of a convert are traced only after the mother, as derived from 'כי יסיר את בנך' (when he turns away your son), and therefore they were permitted to Jacob."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:06:38.968149607Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}